<title>UK: LME copper ends stronger, others follow.</title>
<headline>LME copper ends stronger, others follow.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Bursts higher on firm spreads, but stalls below main barrier of $1,970. Cash threes last at $42/46 vs $37 Wednesday.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Pops up, probes $1,500 resistance.</p>
<p>NICKEL - Jumps, confronts $7,450 ceiling. TIN - Ends firmer.</p>
<p>LEAD - Little changed. ZINC - Finishes slightly higher.</p>
<p>ALLOY- Stronger along with primary market.</p>
</text>
